68-021-01045-6</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pii">10.1186/s40168-021-01045-6</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Dubilier N, Bergin C, Lott C. Symbiotic diversity in marine animals: The art of harnessing chemosynthesis. Nat Rev Microbiol. 2008;6(10):725&#x2013;740. doi: 10.1038/nrmicro1992.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nrmicro1992</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18794911</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Williams A, Rona P. Two new caridean shrimps (bresiliidae) from a hydrothermal field on the Mid- Atlantic Ridge. J Crustac Biol. 1986;6(3):446&#x2013;462. doi: 10.2307/1548184.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.2307/1548184</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Segonzac M, de Saint Laurent M, Casanova B. L'&#xe9;nigme du comportement trophique des crevettes Alviocarididae des sites hydrothermaux de la dorsale m&#xe9;dio-atlantique. Cah Biol Mar. 1993;34:535&#x2212;71.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Zbinden M, Cambon-Bonavita M. Rimicaris exoculata: biology and ecology of a shrimp from deep-sea hydrothermal vents associated with ectosymbiotic bacteria. Mar Ecol Prog Ser Inter-Res Sci Center. 2020;652:187&#x2013;222.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Schmidt C, Le Bris N, Gaill F. Interactions of deep-sea vent invertebrates with their environment: the case of Rimicaris exoculata. J Shellfish Res. 2008;27(1):79&#x2013;90. doi: 10.2983/0730-8000(2008)27[79:IODVIW]2.0.CO;2.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.2983/0730-8000(2008)27[79:IODVIW]2.0.CO;2</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Zbinden M, Le Bris N, Gaill F, Comp&#xe8;re P. Distribution of bacteria and associated minerals in the gill chamber of the vent shrimp Rimicaris exoculata and related biogeochemical processes. Mar Ecol Prog Ser. 2004;284:237&#x2013;251. doi: 10.3354/meps284237.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="