-3</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">23494624</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Savvas S., Donnelly J., Patterson T., Chong Z. S., Esteves S. R. Biological methanation of CO2 in a novel biofilm plug- flow reactor: a high rate and low parasitic energy process. Applied Energy. 2017;202:238&#x2013;247. doi: 10.1016/j.apenergy.2017.05.134.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.apenergy.2017.05.134</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Peprah M., Kougias P. G., Tsapekos P., Treu L., Campanaro S., Angelidaki I. Ex-situ biogas upgrading in thermophilic reactors using membranes as gas diffusion devices. Abstract from 16th IWA World Conference on Anaerobic Digestion; 2019; Delft, Netherlands. pp. 3&#x2013;5.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Agneessens L. M., Ottosen L. D. M., Voigt N. V., et al. In-situ biogas upgrading with pulse H2 additions: the relevance of methanogen adaption and inorganic carbon level. Bioresource Technology. 2017;233:256&#x2013;263. doi: 10.1016/j.biortech.2017.02.016.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.biortech.2017.02.016</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28285216</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wahid R., Mulat D. G., Gaby J. C., Horn S. J. Effects of H2:CO2 ratio and H2 supply fluctuation on methane content and microbial community composition during in-situ biological biogas upgrading. Biotechnology for Biofuels. 2019;12(1):1&#x2013;15. doi: 10.1186/s13068-019-1443-6.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1186/s13068-019-1443-6</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6489297</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31164923</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Corbellini V., Catenacci A., Malpei F. Hydrogenotrophic biogas upgrading integrated into WWTPs: enrichment strategy. Water Science and Technology. 2019;79(4):759&#x2013;770. doi: 10.2166/wst.2019.096.</Citation><ArticleIdLis